---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import { fetchGithubStars, formatStarCount } from "../github";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const stars = await fetchGithubStars();
const starsLabel = stars === null ? "Star" : formatStarCount(stars);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy · Rakazo"
  description="How Inbox Zero Inc. collects, uses, and protects information when you use Rakazo."
>
  <div class="container">
    <Header starsLabel={starsLabel} />
    <main id="main" class="privacy-copy">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p><strong>Last updated: September 14, 2026</strong></p>
      <p>
        This policy explains how Inbox Zero Inc. (“Inbox Zero,” “we,” or “us”) handles personal information
        when you use the Rakazo mobile app, a Rakazo service that we host, or rakazo.com. A third party that
        operates a self-hosted Rakazo deployment is responsible for its own privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you use Rakazo, we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Contact and account information, such as your name, email address, and authentication records.</li>
        <li>
          Content you provide to the service, including bot instructions, messages, tasks, memories, files,
          routines, and support communications.
        </li>
        <li>
          Connection information you choose to provide, such as encrypted credentials or tokens for model
          providers, connected applications, and browser sessions.
        </li>
        <li>
          Technical information needed to operate and secure the service, such as IP address, user agent,
          session records, device push token, timestamps, and diagnostic information.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use this information to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide, maintain, secure, and troubleshoot Rakazo.</li>
        <li>Authenticate you and synchronize your account across supported clients.</li>
        <li>Run the bots, routines, connections, and notifications you request.</li>
        <li>Respond to support requests and comply with legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Service providers and AI processing</h2>
      <p>
        Before submitting content or starting AI work, the Rakazo mobile app names configured
        recipients, explains the data and purpose, and asks you to allow sharing. Choosing Not now
        prevents the mobile action. Permission applies to the selected Space and recipient.
        Account → AI data sharing lets you withdraw permission for new mobile actions.
        Stop existing runs and disable routines separately; withdrawal cannot recall data already
        sent. Web, desktop, and self-hosted server workflows use the connections you configure
        without this mobile permission flow.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Models and agents:</strong> messages, relevant conversation history, bot instructions,
          memories, attachments and file content, screenshots, and content retrieved from connected
          apps are used to generate responses and perform your tasks, including scheduled tasks.
          Supported connections include OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, OpenRouter, Vercel AI Gateway, Cursor, and custom
          model servers. The mobile permission screen identifies the services configured for your Space;
          configuring a service does not by itself grant permission for new mobile actions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>AI gateways:</strong> OpenRouter and Vercel AI Gateway receive requests and forward
          them to model providers according to the connection's routing settings. The mobile
          disclosure names the configured gateway. Processing, retention, and routing depend on
          the gateway account settings and applicable provider agreements. Rakazo's mobile
          permission flow does not change those settings or promise zero retention.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Voice:</strong> recorded audio is sent to your selected transcription service;
          text you choose to play, including bot responses, is sent for speech generation. Supported
          voice services include OpenAI, ElevenLabs, Cartesia, and Fish Audio. Microphone access
          and permission to share with an AI service are separate choices.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Memory:</strong> when Supermemory is configured, conversation summaries, saved
          memories, search queries, and bot and Space identifiers are sent to store and retrieve context. Self-hosted memory
          is processed by the server shown in your permission screen.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We collect this content from what you enter, upload, record, or authorize your bots to access.
        We store the recipient, Space, disclosure version, and time of your permission for the mobile app to remember
        your choices. We do not sell personal information or use Rakazo content for third-party advertising.
      </p>
      <p>
        Services we select to process personal information must provide protection equal to or
        greater than the safeguards described in this policy, including limited processing purposes,
        appropriate security, and retention and deletion protections. Before enabling a provider,
        we review its terms and safeguards against these requirements. A self-hosted operator is
        responsible for assessing the services it selects and its own agreements with those services.
      </p>
      <p>
        Provider terms govern their processing and retention after receipt. You can review the
        applicable provider policy from AI data sharing. Policies for supported services:
        <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/">OpenAI</a>,
        <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy">Anthropic</a>,
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google</a>,
        <a href="https://openrouter.ai/privacy">OpenRouter</a>,
        <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel</a>,
        <a href="https://cursor.com/privacy">Cursor</a>,
        <a href="https://elevenlabs.io/privacy-policy">ElevenLabs</a>,
        <a href="https://cartesia.ai/legal/privacy">Cartesia</a>,
        <a href="https://fish.audio/privacy/">Fish Audio</a>, and
        <a href="https://supermemory.ai/privacy">Supermemory</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Other services may host infrastructure, run sandboxes, deliver notifications, store data,
        or connect apps as needed for the work you request. Connected apps receive the content
        required for the actions you authorize. Their processing is governed by their applicable
        terms and privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Self-hosted deployments</h2>
      <p>
        The Rakazo mobile app can connect to a server that you or another organization operates. In that case,
        the server operator, not Inbox Zero, controls the information sent to that deployment. The app stores the
        selected server address and session token securely on your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        We keep hosted account information and content while your account is active and as reasonably needed to
        provide the service. You can permanently delete your hosted account and associated personal Space
        data from the Account screen in the Rakazo app. We may retain limited information when required by law,
        to resolve disputes, or to enforce agreements. Information already sent to a third-party provider is
        subject to that provider’s retention practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Security and international transfers</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards designed to protect personal information. No
        system is completely secure. We and our service providers may process information in the United States
        and other countries, which may have different data-protection laws than your country.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Rakazo is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from
        children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or receive a copy
        of your personal information, or to object to certain processing. Contact us to make a request.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        Inbox Zero Inc.<br />
        131 Continental Dr, Suite 305<br />
        Newark, Delaware 19713, United States<br />
        <a href="mailto:hello@rakazo.com">hello@rakazo.com</a>
      </p>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
